# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the MAANTA Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v2.0.0)
- Used `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts with existing Vite dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json`

### 2. Configuration
Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout's body section
- Placed after the existing `<PostHogClientProvider>` to maintain proper render order

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the framework-specific integration for Next.js v13.5+:

1. The project uses Next.js 14.2.35 with the App Router (`src/app/` structure)
2. Imported the `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (the Next.js-specific export)
3. Added the component directly in the root layout's body section as recommended for Next.js App Router

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:

✅ **TypeScript Type Check**: Passed with no errors
✅ **ESLint**: No linting warnings or errors
✅ **Unit Tests**: All 221 tests passed (37 test files)
✅ **Build**: Production build completed successfully (exit code 0)

Note: Build warnings about missing Clerk API keys are expected in a build environment without environment variables and are unrelated to the Speed Insights changes.

## Next Steps

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. The Speed Insights script will automatically be injected at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
3. Performance metrics will start being collected automatically
4. View metrics in the Vercel dashboard's Speed Insights section

The implementation preserves all existing functionality and follows the project's code structure and conventions.
